  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improving Transparency and Accountability for Property Rights&apos; Administration in Honduras</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objective of the IDF proposal is to improve transparency and accountability of the land administration sector in Honduras. This objective will be achieved through (i) development of an integrated system for financial management for the Property Institute and its property registries across the country; (ii) implementing a sector-wide management system based on quality and efficiency principles (applying ISO 9001:2000/ EFQM); and (ii) setting up an accountability system including filing and follow up of citizen&apos;s complains and periodic client satisfaction surveys. The objective of the IDF proposal is to improve transparency and accountability of the land administration sector in Honduras. This objective will be achieved through (i) development of an integrated system for financial management for the Property Institute and selected property registries across the country; (ii) implementing a sector-wide management system based on quality and efficiency principles (applying ISO 9001:2000/ EFQM); and (iii) setting up an accountability system, including specifically a tool to file and follow up of citizen&apos;s complains and  client satisfaction surveys. Thisobjective will be achieved through (i) development of an integrated system for financial management for the Property Institute and selected property registries across the country; (ii) implementing a sector-wide management system based on quality and efficiency principles (applying ISO 9001:2000/ EFQM); and (iii) setting up an accountability system, including specifically a tool to file and follow up of citizen&apos;s complains and client satisfaction surveys.</narrative>
  </description>
